This is a very interesting discussion.  I believe you're correct about
these problems.  My first instinct was to agree that a winning bot is
impossible in practice, because a "likelihood-of-survival" function
would depend on far too many things.  But that may just mean this is
the wrong way to go about things.

Machine learning is also not going to help.  So many things happen in
Nethack that no existing automatic technique has a prayer of guessing
which ones are important, let alone how to elicit or avoid them.

